This is an example Play Application using play-swagger with sbt-play-swagger plugin.

The example uses the play-swagger code in this repository, not a released
version. Its project/plugins.sbt refers to version 0.0.1-EXAMPLE, so you must
publish that version locally before you build the example.

1. From the repository root, publish the library and the plugin locally:

     sbt publishForExample

2. Go to the example directory and run the tests. The tests also generate
   the spec:

     cd example
     sbt test

3. To see the generated spec, start the application:

     sbt run

   The spec is at http://localhost:9000/assets/swagger.json
   The Swagger UI is at http://localhost:9000/docs/swagger-ui/index.html
   (enter /assets/swagger.json in the top bar of the UI to load the spec).

Do step 1 again each time you change the code in core or sbtPlugin.
